[2026-03-14T21:30:23.970Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QMX6x1YRPsyCEXSj3cqz6w","type":"tool_result","content":"127-\n128-#### Test: Sidebar renders main navigation links\n129-- **Initial state**: User is authenticated and on `/my-issues`\n130:- **Expected**: The sidebar shows \"My Issues\" with a user-circle icon and \"Inbox\" with an inbox icon. Both are clickable navigation links.\n131-\n132-#### Test: Sidebar My Issues link navigates correctly\n133:- **Initial state**: User is authenticated and on `/inbox`\n134-- **Action**: User clicks \"My Issues\" in the sidebar\n135-- **Expected**: User is navigated to `/my-issues`. The \"My Issues\" link appears selected/active with visual distinction (e.g., highlighted background).\n136-\n137:#### Test: Sidebar Inbox link navigates correctly\n138-- **Initial state**: User is authenticated and on `/my-issues`\n139:- **Action**: User clicks \"Inbox\" in the sidebar\n140:- **Expected**: User is navigated to `/inbox`. The \"Inbox\" link appears selected/active.\n141-\n142:#### Test: Sidebar Inbox shows unread notification count badge\n143-- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, has 3 unread notifications\n144:- **Expected**: The \"Inbox\" link in the sidebar displays a badge showing \"3\". The badge is visually distinct (e.g., accent color background).\n145-\n146:#### Test: Sidebar Inbox badge updates when notifications are read\n147-- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, has 3 unread notifications, badge shows \"3\"\n148:- **Action**: User navigates to `/inbox` and marks one notification as read\n149-- **Expected**: The badge count updates to \"2\". If all notifications are read, the badge disappears.\n150-\n151:#### Test: Sidebar Inbox badge not shown when no unread notifications\n152-- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, has 0 unread notifications\n153:- **Expected**: No badge is shown next to the \"Inbox\" link.\n154-\n155-#### Test: Sidebar renders team sections\n156-- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, workspace has teams \"Engineering\" and \"Design\"\n--\n221-\n222-#### Test: Sidebar active highlight updates on navigation\n223-- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, on `/my-issues`, \"My Issues\" is highlighted\n224:- **Action**: User clicks \"Inbox\" in the sidebar\n225:- **Expected**: \"Inbox\" becomes highlighted and \"My Issues\" loses its highlight.\n226-\n227-#### Test: Sidebar is present on all authenticated pages\n228-- **Initial state**: User is authenticated\n229:- **Action**: User navigates to `/my-issues`, then `/inbox`, then `/settings`\n230-- **Expected**: The sidebar is visible and functional on all three pages with consistent layout and content.\n231-\n232-#### Test: Sidebar is not shown on login page\n--\n257-\n258-#### Test: Sidebar collapse state persists across navigation\n259-- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, sidebar is collapsed to icon-only mode\n260:- **Action**: User clicks the \"My Issues\" icon in the collapsed sidebar, then clicks the \"Inbox\" icon\n261-- **Expected**: The sidebar remains in collapsed icon-only mode through both navigations. It does not re-expand on page change.\n262-\n263-#### Test: Sidebar icons are still clickable in collapsed mode\n264-- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, sidebar is in icon-only mode, user is on `/my-issues`\n265:- **Action**: User clicks the Inbox icon in the collapsed sidebar\n266:- **Expected**: User is navigated to `/inbox`. The navigation works identically to the expanded sidebar.\n267-\n268-#### Test: Sidebar collapse toggle works multiple times in sequence\n269-- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, sidebar is expanded\n--\n291-- **Expected**: The character \"c\" is typed into the input field. The create issue modal does NOT open.\n292-\n293-#### Test: G then I navigates to My Issues\n294:- **Initial state**: User is authenticated and on `/inbox`, focus is not in a text input\n295-- **Action**: User presses \"G\" key, then presses \"I\" key\n296-- **Expected**: User is navigated to `/my-issues`.\n297-\n298:#### Test: G then N navigates to Inbox\n299-- **Initial state**: User is authenticated and on `/my-issues`, focus is not in a text input\n300-- **Action**: User presses \"G\" key, then presses \"N\" key\n301:- **Expected**: User is navigated to `/inbox`.\n302-\n303-#### Test: G then I does not navigate when typing in input\n304-- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, focus is in a text input field\n--\n488-- **Action**: User clicks an issue title to view detail, then navigates back to `/my-issues`\n489-- **Expected**: The filters are still applied showing only \"In Progress\" issues. The filter state is preserved across navigation.\n490-\n491:## Inbox Page (`/inbox`)\n492-\n493-**Components**: NotificationList, NotificationRow\n494-\n495-### NotificationList\n496-\n497:#### Test: Inbox page renders with list of notifications\n498-- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, has 3 notifications (1 assignment, 1 issue update, 1 mention)\n499:- **Expected**: The page displays a header \"Inbox\" at the top. All 3 notifications are listed in reverse chronological order (newest first). Each notification is a distinct row.\n500-\n501:#### Test: Inbox page shows empty state when no notifications\n502-- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, has no notifications\n503-- **Expected**: The page displays a friendly empty state message with an icon (e.g., \"No notifications yet\" or \"You're all caught up!\") instead of an empty list.\n504-\n505:#### Test: Inbox shows unread notifications visually distinct from read\n506-- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, has 2 unread notifications and 1 read notification\n507-- **Expected**: Unread notifications appear with bold text and a left border accent (using the primary accent color `#5e6ad2`). Read notifications appear with normal weight text and no left border accent.\n508-\n509:#### Test: Inbox page shows notification count in header\n510-- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, has 5 unread notifications\n511:- **Expected**: The inbox header or a badge near it indicates the number of unread notifications (e.g., \"Inbox (5)\" or a count badge).\n512-\n513:#### Test: Inbox notification list updates sidebar badge when notifications change\n514:- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, has 3 unread notifications, sidebar Inbox badge shows \"3\"\n515:- **Action**: User marks one notification as read on the inbox page\n516:- **Expected**: The sidebar Inbox badge updates to \"2\".\n517-\n518:#### Test: Inbox notifications are ordered by newest first\n519-- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, has notifications from 5 minutes ago, 1 hour ago, and 1 day ago\n520-- **Expected**: Notifications appear in order: 5 minutes ago (top), 1 hour ago (middle), 1 day ago (bottom).\n521-\n522-#### Test: Archiving a notification removes it from the list\n523:- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, has 3 notifications visible in the inbox\n524-- **Action**: User clicks the archive button/icon on the first notification\n525:- **Expected**: The notification is removed from the inbox list. The list now shows 2 notifications. The archived notification does not reappear.\n526-\n527-#### Test: Archiving multiple notifications works in sequence\n528-- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, has 3 notifications visible\n--\n532-#### Test: All notifications can be archived to reach empty state\n533-- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, has 2 notifications visible\n534-- **Action**: User archives both notifications one by one\n535:- **Expected**: After all notifications are archived, the empty state message is displayed. The sidebar Inbox badge disappears (no unread count).\n536-\n537-### NotificationRow\n538-\n--\n551-#### Test: Clicking an unread notification marks it as read\n552-- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, has an unread notification for issue ENG-42 (bold text, left border accent)\n553-- **Action**: User clicks on the notification row\n554:- **Expected**: The notification's visual style changes from unread (bold, left border accent) to read (normal weight, no left border accent). The change is persisted to the database. The sidebar Inbox badge count decrements by 1.\n555-\n556-#### Test: Clicking a read notification does not change its state\n557-- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, has a read notification (normal weight, no accent)\n--\n564-- **Expected**: User is navigated to `/issue/<issueId>` for issue ENG-42. The issue detail page loads showing ENG-42.\n565-\n566-#### Test: Notification row archive button is visible\n567:- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, has a notification visible in the inbox\n568-- **Expected**: Each notification row has an archive button/icon (e.g., an archive or x icon) visible on hover or always visible, allowing the user to archive the notification.\n569-\n570-#### Test: Notification row archive button archives without navigating\n571:- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, viewing the inbox with a notification for ENG-42\n572-- **Action**: User clicks the archive button on the ENG-42 notification row\n573:- **Expected**: The notification is archived and removed from the list. The user remains on the `/inbox` page — no navigation to the issue detail occurs. The archive action is persisted to the database.\n574-\n575-#### Test: Notification row shows correct icon per notification type\n576-- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, has one of each notification type: assignment, issue update, mention\n--\n586-- **Expected**: The notification is first marked as read (visual change), then archived and removed from the list. Both actions succeed in sequence without conflict.\n587-\n588-#### Test: Notification row click and archive button have separate hit targets\n589:- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, has a notification in the inbox\n590-- **Action**: User clicks specifically on the archive button area of a notification row\n591-- **Expected**: Only the archive action fires — the notification is archived. The user does NOT navigate to the issue detail page. The click targets for \"mark as read + navigate\" and \"archive\" are clearly separated.\n592-\n--\n1418-- **Action**: User creates an issue with title \"Track history\" and clicks \"Create Issue\"\n1419-- **Expected**: When viewing the new issue's detail page, the Activity tab shows an initial \"created this issue\" entry with the current user's name and timestamp.\n1420-\n1421:#### Test: Created issue generates inbox notification for assignee\n1422-- **Initial state**: Create issue modal is open. Current user is \"Alice Smith\".\n1423-- **Action**: User creates an issue with title \"Review PR\", assigns it to \"Bob Jones\", and clicks \"Create Issue\"\n1424:- **Expected**: When Bob Jones checks their inbox, a notification appears: \"Alice Smith assigned you to [issue identifier]: Review PR\" with the correct timestamp. The inbox badge count increases.\n1425-\n1426-#### Test: Create Issue button is disabled during submission\n1427-- **Initial state**: Create issue modal is open with valid data entered"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_015qryzSujPT5PpuZiGzYCdJ","session_id":"8c773c69-5b70-4948-a5ae-cf557e586ea9","uuid":"d82d052d-413f-4f81-a16f-3d60ed8e7b41"}
